    "authored-1": {
      "id": "authored-1",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The prompt-editor turns a human annotation queue into structured proposals against a target PromptDocument. A human accepts or rejects each staged change; direct external MCP saves use a separate lifecycle."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "authored-2": {
      "id": "authored-2",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Contract"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "authored-3": {
      "id": "authored-3",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The agent manifest is "
        },
        {
          "insert": "packages/prompt-kit-agent/catalog/prompt-editor/agent.json",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true,
            "reference": {
              "kind": "source",
              "path": "packages/prompt-kit-agent/catalog/prompt-editor/agent.json"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ". It selects the prompt-editor model alias with low thinking, a 40-turn limit, and extensions disabled. The harness mounts its own catalog, where prompt-editor can edit itself."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "authored-4": {
      "id": "authored-4",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The canonical behavior prompt lives in "
        },
        {
          "insert": "packages/prompt-kit-agent/catalog/prompt-editor/prompt/prompt.json",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true,
            "reference": {
              "kind": "source",
              "path": "packages/prompt-kit-agent/catalog/prompt-editor/prompt/prompt.json"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ". Its system.md file is generated output; changes belong in the structured prompt."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "authored-5": {
      "id": "authored-5",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Context and State"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "authored-6": {
      "id": "authored-6",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The context sidecar assembles prompt_kit_authoring from current native Docs standards through the shared guidance renderer. Local tool_guide and state_reference blocks retain internal tool semantics. The context is session-invariant; it does not read the live request queue."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "authored-7": {
      "id": "authored-7",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The state sidecar carries targetAgent, targetPromptRender, targetPromptHash, appliedDiffs, and requestQueue. It renders the current target, applied diffs, and R-alias requests for each session. A missing context source remains an explicit status rather than silently substituting unrelated guidance."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "authored-8": {
      "id": "authored-8",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Context assembly is defined by "
        },
        {
          "insert": "packages/prompt-kit-agent/catalog/prompt-editor/context/index.ts",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true,
            "reference": {
              "kind": "source",
              "path": "packages/prompt-kit-agent/catalog/prompt-editor/context/index.ts"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": "; live state is defined by "
        },
        {
          "insert": "packages/prompt-kit-agent/catalog/prompt-editor/state/index.ts",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true,
            "reference": {
              "kind": "source",
              "path": "packages/prompt-kit-agent/catalog/prompt-editor/state/index.ts"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": "."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "authored-9": {
      "id": "authored-9",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Tools and Output"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "authored-10": {
      "id": "authored-10",
      "type": "structured-table",
      "props": {
        "columns": [
          "Tool",
          "Internal effect"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            "read_prompt",
            "Read the current target with stable IDs."
          ],
          [
            "propose_transaction",
            "Compile and stage a structural edit for human review."
          ],
          [
            "resolve_request",
            "Resolve one annotation request."
          ],
          [
            "reply_request",
            "Reply to a request thread."
          ],
          [
            "add_note",
            "Attach a note to the session."
          ]
        ]
      },
      "children": []
    },
    "authored-11": {
      "id": "authored-11",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The session service binds these tools per spawn. A proposal does not save merely because compilation succeeds. Acceptance uses the shared store; a stale base must be reconciled, and accepted changes retain the internal review and undo behavior."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "state-fixtures": {
      "id": "state-fixtures",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "State fixtures under state/fixtures contain data-only envelopes with an optional label and a state sample of PromptEditorState. The lab passes the state sample to render() for section ③; fixtures are not context sessionData and real spawns seed state from the session service instead."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    }
  }
